missing predicate keys by returning a \"range\" error, which is appropriate since without `from_seq` and `to_seq` we can't determine the expected count. This is fine because in the actual monitor code, the predicate comes from a verified Rekor attestation, so it should always have the required keys.\n\nLet me also run a quick test to ensure the monitor command integration would work correctly by simulating the check.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The function handles missing predicate keys by returning a \\\"range\\\" error, which is appropriate since without `from_seq` and `to_seq` we can't determine the expected count. This is fine because in the actual monitor code, the predicate comes from a verified Rekor attestation, so it should always have the required keys.\\n\\nLet me also run a quick test to ensure the monitor command integration would work correctly by simulating the check.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The function handles edge cases appropriately. Let me verify the monitor integration by looking at the final implementation once more:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-04e4eaff-82aa-4b7b-ae20-ccd2545f039e","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":40,"offset":300,"path":"/workspace/record/record.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":4057,"output":162,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":87,"totalTokens":30523,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794513882029,"responseId":"gen-1794513882-749ozjyWpSbY0HedY6Zn","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":10132,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-04e4eaff-82aa-4b7b-ae20-ccd2545f039e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    return {\"from_seq\": from_seq, \"to_seq\": to_seq,\n            \"prev_sha256\": chain[from_seq - 2][1] if from_seq > 1 else None, \"head_sha256\": chain[to_seq - 1][1]}\n\n\ndef _orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Validate the entries hidden by an orphan against the attested predicate.\n    Returns None if valid, else a short problem string containing 'range', 'chain', or 'head'.\"\"\"\n    entries_b64 = orphan.get(\"body\", {}).get(\"entries_b64\", [])\n    from_seq = pred.get(\"from_seq\")\n    to_seq = pred.get(\"to_seq\")\n    expected_count = to_seq - from_seq + 1 if from_seq is not None and to_seq is not None else -1\n    \n    if len(entries_b64) != expected_count:\n        return f\"range: expected {expected_count} entries, got {len(entries_b64)}\"\n    \n    prev_sha256 = pred.get(\"prev_sha256\")\n    head_sha256 = pred.get(\"head_sha256\")\n    \n    for i, entry_b64 in enumerate(entries_b64):\n        try:\n            entry_raw = base64.b64decode(entry_b64, validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            return f\"chain: entry {i} is not valid base64\"\n        \n        entry = parse_json(entry_raw, f\"orphan entry {i}\")\n        if entry.get(\"prev\") != prev_sha256:\n            return f\"chain: entry {i} prev {entry.get('prev')!r} != expected {prev_sha256!r}\"\n        prev_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(entry_raw).hexdigest()\n    \n    if prev_sha256 != head_sha256:\n        return f\"head: last entry sha256 {prev_sha256!r} != attested head {head_sha256!r}\"\n    \n    return None\n\n\ndef check_sigstore(bundle, digest, repo, workflow, ref):\n    \"\"\"Verify offline that a bundle is an attestation of this digest, signed by exactly this workflow on this ref.\n    Returns (integrated_time, predicate). Wrong data is Bad; a missing library is CantCheck.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from sigstore.models import Bundle\n\n[303 more lines in file. Use offset=340 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":2,"timestamp":1794513892163},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The function loo