ror string containing `\"chain\"` if an entry's `prev` doesn't link properly\n   - Returns error string containing `\"head\"` if the last entry's sha256 doesn't match `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`\n\n3. **Wired into `cmd_monitor`**: After verifying an orphan's statement matches Rekor's payload, the function is called to validate the hidden entries against the predicate. If validation fails, the orphan is reported as \"wrong\" with a descriptive error message."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":2952,"output":282,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":14,"totalTokens":33922,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794513903435,"responseId":"gen-1794513903-HX6SV2VrqWz8wK7heIZF","rawStopReason":"stop","durationMs":6184,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"willRetry":false}
